  #[#set math.equation(numbering: n => "(7.25)")
   $ h^0 \( Delta_F \, cal(L) \) lt.eq R \/ 4 . $ <eq:frob-diagonal-rank>]
  Thus the rank of (7.19) is at most $R \/ 4$ at every point of the diagonal.
  #emph[The determinant contradiction.] Choose $R$ columns of (7.19) with nonzero determinant,
    and write $a_i^(\( nu \))$ for the weight of slot $i$ in column $nu$.
    Their determinant is a nonzero section of the external product of the line bundles
  $ cal(Q)_i = \( det cal(E) \)^(⊗ R \/ s) ⊗ cal(O)_(W') (sum_(nu = 1)^R a_i^(\( nu \)) K_(W')) . $
  Let $lambda_i = R^(- 1) sum_(nu = 1)^R a_i^(\( nu \))$; then $0 lt.eq lambda_i lt.eq q$.
    Identifying numerical classes through base-field twist, we have
  #[#set math.equation(numbering: n => "(7.26)")
   $ frac(c_1 \( cal(Q)_i \), R) = B / p + (frac(p - 1, 2 p) + lambda_i) K_W . $ <eq:frob-determinant-class>]
