  $ c_1 \( F^(*) cal(E) \) = s B + frac(s \( p - 1 \), 2) K_W . $
  Relative Frobenius pullback multiplies divisor classes by $p$ after the base-twist identification.
    Since the determinant of $cal(E)^(times.square t)$ contributes $\( det cal(E) \)^(R \/ s)$ in each slot,
